<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<!--
	Global gatekeeper content, used by the script.teleport.GlobalGatekeeper script.

	<settings>
		rowsPerPage      : amount of rows shown per page, on every generated list.
		popularLimit     : amount of points kept on the "popular" tab.
		popularMinCount  : minimum amount of teleports for a point to enter the "popular" tab.
		karmaPriceRate   : price multiplier applied on chaotic (PK) players. 1 means no penalty.
		defaultPriceId   : default currency, inherited by menus, tabs, areas and points.
		defaultPrice     : default price of STANDARD points, inherited by menus, tabs, areas and points.
		defaultNoblePrice: default price of NOBLE points, inherited the same way.
		goLabel          : label of the teleport link, on the action column.
		nobleLabel       : label shown instead of the link, when the point requires noblesse.
		lockedLabel      : label shown instead of the link, when the point is out of reach.
		freeLabel        : label shown on the price column, when the teleport is free.
		emptyLabel       : label shown instead of an empty list.

	<npc>
		id / menu : binds a npc id to a menu id. Add a line to make any npc a gatekeeper.

	<menu>
		Holds the tabs of the dialog. Multiple npcs can share a menu. priceId / price / noblePrice
		can be set on <menu>, <item>, <area> and <loc> - the closest definition wins.

	<item> (a tab of the top bar)
		- holding <area> nodes    : generates the areas list page (areas.htm).
		- type="popular"          : generates the most used points page (popular.htm).
		- page="somefile.htm"     : shows an additional datapack HTM of the script folder.
		- bypass="..."            : any regular bypass, handled by the core (multisell, quest, ...).
		name / color              : label and color of the tab. %objectId% is supported on bypasses.

	<loc>
		id       : unique id, used as database key of the teleport counter. Never reuse it.
		name     : location name, shown on the first column.
		point    : optional sub-point name, shown on the second column.
		type     : STANDARD or NOBLE (requires a noblesse player).
		x / y / z: destination.
		castleId : optional, forbids the teleport while the castle siege is in progress.
		minLevel / maxLevel : optional level restriction.
-->
<list>
